From b435c184c18637939e862e0349d225a6b16cb4f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Francesco Pham <francesco.pham1@h-partners.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 12:50:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] runtime_core: keep the LLVM backend off on x86_64 device
 products

OpenHarmony-7.0 narrowed the x86_64 LLVM backend opt-out to is_emulator.
x86_general is an x86_64 device product built with is_emulator = false,
so it now takes the LLVM irtoc path, whose interpreter_inline.bc step
runs llvm-link from prebuilts/ark_tools/llvm_aot/aot_gn_ohos -- a
prebuilt that only carries headers and libLLVM, so ninja stops with
"missing and no known rule to make it".

Restore the OpenHarmony-6.1 behaviour of disabling the LLVM backend for
non-standalone x86_64 builds.

Change-Id: I48a6b326880ed84f443c3f9785e0b55c6af188ff
Signed-off-by: Francesco Pham <francesco.pham1@h-partners.com>
---
 static_core/ark_config.gni | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/static_core/ark_config.gni b/static_core/ark_config.gni
index 7bd4cbf98c..98a6be63c6 100644
--- a/static_core/ark_config.gni
+++ b/static_core/ark_config.gni
@@ -228,6 +228,19 @@ if (target_cpu == "arm64") {
   is_llvm_aot = false
 }
 
+# The LLVM backend is only exercised on x86_64 by emulator builds, which
+# disable it above; an x86_64 device product (is_emulator = false) would
+# otherwise need an llvm-link from aot_gn_ohos, which only ships headers
+# and libLLVM.  OpenHarmony-6.1 disabled it for every non-standalone x86_64
+# build; keep doing so.
+if (!ark_static_standalone_build &&
+    (target_cpu == "x64" || target_cpu == "x86_64")) {
+  is_llvmbackend = false
+  is_llvm_interpreter = false
+  is_llvm_fastpath = false
+  is_llvm_aot = false
+}
+
 if (panda_runtime_sdk_build) {
   is_llvmbackend = false
   is_llvm_interpreter = false
-- 
